ent accounting bases (AMD: GAAP; NVIDIA: non-GAAP), so they are not like for like. Say so."], "clean": true}}, "run_dir": "experiments/results/model_compare_v1/runs/20261012-024856_reliability_compare-the-gross-margins-of-nvidia-fiscal-year", "answered": true, "facts_found": ["NVIDIA FY2025 gross margin 75.0% GAAP (75.5% non-GAAP)", "AMD FY2024 gross margin 49% GAAP (53% non-GAAP)"], "facts_missed": ["Intel FY2024 gross margin 32.7% GAAP (36.0% non-GAAP)"], "fact_recall": 0.667, "fact_recall_in_evidence": 0.667, "coverage_missed": [], "coverage": 1.0, "grounding": 1.0, "quality": 0.889, "cites_authoritative_source": true, "v2": {"quality_v1": 0.889, "grounding": 1.0, "rules": [], "not_found_credit": [], "misattributed": [], "facts_found": ["NVIDIA FY2025 gross margin 75.0% GAAP (75.5% non-GAAP)", "AMD FY2024 gross margin 49% GAAP (53% non-GAAP)"], "fact_recall": 0.667, "coverage": 1.0, "ordering_errors": [], "quality": 0.889}, "gaps": "no evidence for: Intel gross margin performance for fiscal year 2024; comparison caveat: the figures are on different accounting bases (AMD: GAAP; NVIDIA: non-GAAP), so they are not like for like. Say so.", "ref_model_seconds": 326.7, "observed_gen_tps": 17.7}
